===persian===

من از تو سیر نخواهم شد....
کویر از باران...
و دشت از آهو...
و کوه از تیهو...
مُریدِ چشم توام...
کف به دَف زَنَم
هو... هو...
بهار ۱۳۷۳

===machine===

I will never have my fill of you....
nor the desert of the rain...
nor the plain of the gazelle...
nor the mountain of the partridge...
I am the disciple of your eyes...
Let me strike my palm on the daf —
hu... hu...
Spring 1373

===lantern===

I will never have my fill of you —
no more than the desert of rain,
or the plain of the gazelle,
or the mountain of the partridge.
I am the disciple of your eyes.
Let me strike my palm on the daf:
hu... hu...

Spring 1373

===translation===

===footnotes===

هو — *Hu*, 'He' — is the syllable of the Sufi dhikr, chanted to the frame drum until the
word and the breath are the same thing. The poem arrives there in three lines from a list of
thirsts, and the beloved's eyes have become the order the poet has joined.
